{
  "article": "The daughter of one of Europe’s longest-reigning monarchs, known for her psychic abilities, has tied the knot with a self-proclaimed sixth-generation shaman from California. Princess Märtha Louise of Norway's wedding to Durek Verrett on Saturday was not a typical royal event, but it nevertheless drew observers to the cloudy streets of Geiranger, eager to catch a view of the bride. Märtha Louise, the sole daughter of King Harald and Queen Sonja, at 52 years old, ranks fourth in line for the Norwegian crown. The couple wed in a Church of Norway ceremony at the four-star Hotel Union, attended by royalty and celebrities, set in a quaint village near the Geiranger fjord. The princess was accompanied by seven bridesmaids, among them were her teenage daughters Leah and Emma Behn from her first marriage with Norwegian author Ari Behn, who passed away after they divorced in 2017. Among the 350 attendees were Märtha Louise’s sibling, Crown Prince Haakon, and his spouse, Crown Princess Mette-Marit; Sweden’s Crown Princess Victoria and her spouse, Prince Daniel; and Prince Constantijn and Princess Laurentien from the Netherlands. Known for leading an unconventional life, Princess Märtha Louise has identified as a clairvoyant and ran a healing school for a decade where she guided individuals to communicate with angels. She announced in 2022 her decision to step back from official royal responsibilities, choosing to concentrate on her joint business ventures with Verret and to more distinctly separate their endeavors from the Norwegian royal family. Verrett, on his Instagram profile, describes himself as a “servant of God” and “energy activator”, with notable clients, including Gwyneth Paltrow, the founder of Goop, whom he regards as a “soul sister”."
}
```

